  "comparison_axes": {
    "contour": "Hard angular shield and uniform pill outlines differ from rounded painted motif edges and draped cloth.",
    "material": "Shield/pills have flat fills; dog/butterfly and banner show brush/shading/stitched or fabric cues.",
    "palette": "Saved purple/gold and pastel room hues correspond; the dark blue full-screen overlay is a separate strong field. Hue agreement alone does not establish style congruency.",
    "light": "Motif highlights and banner fold shadows have authored directional form; uniform shield panels lack comparable material modelling.",
    "perspective": "Preview is frontal; room banners are frontal wall hangings. Cloth is a plausible reuse candidate, but a layout trial is needed to retain the shield/badge semantics.",
    "scale": "Large preview is readable on desktop; small selector glyphs and room motifs need actual phone/device squint acceptance. Targets retain source dimensions at both widths.",
    "contact": "Room banners have source rods/fixtures. Center motif sits on a medallion; no new shadow or contact was invented. Badge backing remains visually separate from paper board.",
    "occlusion": "Both registered room pairs show the selected motif. Craft badge remains. Global Back/title and transient toast/color overlap remain; wide room margins remain visible.",
    "readability": "Dog/butterfly menu imagery differs from preview artwork. Selected color and highlighted tile are visible; eight exact-source thumbnails are a bounded reuse route. Non-reader/child acceptance is pending.",
    "action_state": "48 combinations per aspect use original controls; passive/pressed/released/cancel/Keep/background/fresh-Main reload are retained. Discrete snapshots do not establish full animation/contact playback or OS/device lifecycle."
  },
